Error [E-TYPE-PREFIX]: `?T` and `!E` are retired prefix type marks.
  --> tests/ui/type_mark_prefix_optional_retired.jet:4:12
    |
  4 |     tags: [?String]
    |            ^^^^^^^
 Why: A type mark follows the type it marks: `Entry?` may be absent, and `SaveError!` in a function contract names how the call fails.
 Fix: Write `Entry?` for `?Entry`, `SaveError!` for `!SaveError`, and `(A | B)!` for `!(A | B)`.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-TYPE-PREFIX

